{"key":"apbio-mcq-sv-023-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.5-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"A peripheral protein attached to the cytoplasmic face of the plasma membrane","working":"Protein Y is released by a high-salt wash, which selectively releases peripheral proteins held by ionic interactions without disrupting the lipid bilayer. Trypsin, a membrane-impermeable protease, does not cleave Protein Y in intact cells, meaning Protein Y is not exposed on the extracellular surface. However, trypsin does cleave Protein Y when cells are broken open, exposing the intracellular (cytoplasmic) face of the membrane. This demonstrates that Protein Y is located on the cytoplasmic face of the membrane.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":508,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":508,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":745,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":134,"reasoningTokens":611},"totalTokens":1253,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":611,"promptTokenCount":508,"candidatesTokenCount":134,"totalTokenCount":1253,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":508}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":134}]},"reasoningTokens":611,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":47052,"keyed_label":"A"}
